Approach

1.The log file is processed line by line so that large log files can be handled efficiently without loading the entire file into memory.
2.Two dictionaries are used to keep track of counts: one dictionary stores the number of actions performed by each user, and another dictionary stores the frequency of each action.
3.For every log entry, the program splits the line to extract the user_id and action, then updates their counts in the corresponding dictionaries. While updating these counts, the program also keeps track of the user with the highest number of actions and the action with the highest frequency.
4.After processing all log entries, the program returns the most active user and the most common action.
